0..66 Comment "//! One function of a buddy allocator, popping a free block, meets"
67..99 Comment "//! its free-list specification."
100..103 Comment "//!"
104..179 Comment "//! Corten\'s case study verifies a buddy allocator against a representation"
180..258 Comment "//! predicate over Rust\'s value forest. This is its second rung after Corten\'s"
259..335 Comment "//! `example`, a function that reads, matches on and writes through a place."
336..339 Comment "//!"
340..408 Comment "//! The body is THIR written as data, its precondition computed by a"
409..486 Comment "//! weakest-precondition fold over it. A read or a write is an existential, a"
487..560 Comment "//! value the place holds with its equation, so stuck places stay in path"
561..637 Comment "//! endpoints. The proof cases on the free list and carries each equation by"
638..666 Comment "//! `Path.ap` and transport."
667..670 Comment "//!"
671..750 Comment "//! - cites: [Farka-2026-corten_foundational_verification_rust_programs], 2026,"
751..770 Comment "//!   § 3 and § 8"
771..821 Comment "//! - see: corpus/model/interop/thir/example.gandr"
822..825 Comment "//!"
826..990 Comment "//! [Farka-2026-corten_foundational_verification_rust_programs]: https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.04372 \"Farka et al., Corten: Foundational Verification of Rust Programs\""
